<article class="env-remark" id="04JL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04JL">Remark <span data-tag="04JL">59.56.4</span>.</a> Another way to state the conclusion of Theorem <a href="/tag/03QT" data-tag="03QT">59.56.3</a> and Fundamental Groups, Lemma <a href="/tag/03QR" data-tag="03QR">58.2.2</a> is to say that every sheaf on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)_{\acute{e}tale}$ is representable by a scheme $X$ étale over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)$. This does not mean that every sheaf is representable in the sense of Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/00WR" data-tag="00WR">7.12.3</a>. The reason is that in our construction of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)_{\acute{e}tale}$ we chose a sufficiently large set of schemes étale over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)$, whereas sheaves on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)_{\acute{e}tale}$ form a proper class. </p>
</article>